    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 16,
        "line": 1,
        "text": "Though I hadn't seen or spoken to Sheldrake in over thirty years, it seemed impossible that his heart was the thing that had finally failed him..."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 16,
        "line": 1082,
        "text": "Some time later we learned that one of our long boats had been recovered. Several young men found it washed up on a nameless beach somewhere on the island of Hispaniola. No one seemed to know who they were or where they came from, but they seemed to know of the Albatross."
      }
